Priority: P2
Title:    [P2] Remediate /usr/bin/php82 (LIKELY_VULNERABLE, SAPI: cli)
Steps:
  1. No verified Alpine fix is recorded yet; check vendor security trackers for backported package updates.
  2. Temporary configuration mitigation (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):
     Create drop-in INI file /etc/php/conf.d/99-mitigation.ini:
       session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
Commands:
  [Upgrade Alpine PHP packages] apk update && apk upgrade php82-cli php82-fpm php82-common
Restart Hints:
  - reload php-fpm or Apache if web SAPIs share this PHP installation
Notes:    WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.
